                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238299850",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198108383681",
                            "num_reviews": 2037,
                            "playtime_forever": 573,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 573,
                            "last_played": 1791958252
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "'Luxor Evolved' is a fast-paced retro-styled arcade shooter variant of the classic match-three puzzle formula, exchanging the traditional Egyptian backdrops for flashy vector-neon graphics, modern boss battles, and a techno soundtrack.\n\nI can't believe this game has 97% rating on Steam. I know I'm in minority, but I will be honest, as I'm always: I simply hate this game. This is not 'Luxor' anymore, this is something new, 'Pac-Man'ized version of 'Luxor'. I love 'Pac-Man' games, but this is just not working. Also, the marbles are moving too fast, even on Easy level; map layouts are bad, you have no idea where marbles come from or go to. I think the devs forgot what made 'Luxor' a great game, yes, it was those beautifully hand-crafted Ancient Egyptian levels. And most importantly, there's no lifetime statistics.",
